changes.description:
Add directed tests, each checking the retired pc/insn/rd_wdata stream
against the expected program order, rvfi_order +1, and at least one
cycle-count bound showing the zero-bubble win:
  (1) a backward BNE loop run N times: taken iterations after
      warm-up retire back-to-back, and the exit mispredict redirects
      to pc+4;
  (2) a JAL-heavy call chain;
  (3) a branch that alternates taken/not-taken;
  (4) two branches whose PCs share pc[6:2] (index alias) and a
      non-branch at a PC that shares index and tag with a trained
      branch after code is jumped around (pred_taken on a
      non-control instruction must redirect to pc+4);
  (5) a DIV right after a trained-branch alias (the DIV must not be
      flushed);
  (6) the loop from (1) with ~22% random io_imemReady / io_dmemReady
      stalls, producing an identical retirement stream.

